          "screenshot_evidence": "The screenshot shows a ClinicalTrials.gov search results page in a card-style list with a left filter panel titled \u201cFocus Your Search.\u201d In the filter panel, under \u201cStudy Phase,\u201d the checkbox next to \u201cPhase 3 (30)\u201d is visibly checked (blue check). Other phase checkboxes (e.g., Early Phase 1, Phase 1, Phase 2, Phase 4, Not applicable) appear unchecked. The filter panel also shows an \u201cAccepts healthy volunteers\u201d section with \u201cYes (76)\u201d unchecked, and \u201cStudy Type\u201d options (Interventional, Observational, etc.) below. At the bottom of the filter panel are buttons \u201cClear Filters (4)\u201d and \u201cApply Filters.\u201d\n\nIn the results area on the right, at least two study cards are visible. One card shows NCT05899023 with the title \u201cED Diabetes Screening and Outpatient Care - Aim 3\u201d and a green status badge \u201cRecruiting.\u201d It lists locations \u201cNew York, New York, United States.\u201d Another card shows NCT07229482 with the title \u201cPotatoes, Type 2 Diabetes, and Cardiometabolic Health\u201d and also has a green \u201cRecruiting\u201d badge, with location \u201cBlacksburg, Virginia, United States.\u201d A partially visible entry above mentions \u201cMaturity Onset Diabetes of the Young\u201d and location \u201cCincinnati, Ohio, United States,\u201d but its NCT number and status are not fully visible. The top right shows controls including \u201cClear (0),\u201d \u201cDownload,\u201d \u201cSave,\u201d \u201cRSS,\u201d and a \u201cDisplay\u201d button.\n\nNo \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d date text is visible on the study cards in this screenshot, and no visible sort indicator such as \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d or \u201cNewest first\u201d appears in the shown portion.",
          "criterion_analysis": "This screenshot provides evidence that at least one required filter is applied: Study Phase is set to \u201cPhase 3\u201d (checked). The visible study cards show \u201cRecruiting\u201d status and U.S. locations, which is consistent with the required Study Status=Recruiting and Study Location=United States, but the screenshot does not show the Study Status filter control itself nor an explicit \u201cUnited States\u201d location filter selection in the left panel\u2014only that the displayed results have U.S. locations.\n\nCritically, the stopping condition requires that all three filters and the newest-first sorting by \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d are visibly applied, and then the first three displayed results must be recorded with NCT number, full title, study status, and Last Update Posted date. In this screenshot, the \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d date is not shown for any study, and the sorting state (e.g., \u201cLast Update Posted, newest first\u201d) is not visible. Also, only two complete results with NCT numbers are clearly readable (NCT05899023 and NCT07229482); a third result is only partially visible and lacks key fields. Therefore, based on this screenshot alone, the criterion is not fully satisfied: the necessary \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d fields and confirmation of newest-first sorting are not visible, and three complete results are not fully captured.",
          "discrepancies": "The agent\u2019s predicted output is an error (\u201cRunnerError: ChromiumRL.captureStructuredSnapshot timed out...\u201d), which does not report the first three results or any required fields. The screenshot shows at least two recruiting Phase 3 studies with NCT numbers and titles visible, but the agent output contains none of this information. Additionally, the task requires Last Update Posted dates and newest-first sorting confirmation; the screenshot does not display Last Update Posted dates or a visible sorting setting, so any claim of having captured those would not be supported here (though the agent output does not claim it).",
