    "step5_reality_check": {
      "0": "ClinicalTrials.gov shows a left \u201cFocus Your Search\u201d filter panel with checkboxes (including a \u201cStudy Phase\u201d section where \u201cPhase 3\u201d can be checked) and a results header line \u201cSearch Details\u201d that can summarize applied constraints (e.g., \u201ctype 2 diabetes | In United States | Recruiting studies\u201d and sometimes \u201cPhase: 3\u201d). In some screenshots, Phase 3 is clearly checked; in others it is clearly unchecked. The \u201cUnited States\u201d and \u201cRecruiting\u201d constraints are sometimes visible only via the \u201cSearch Details\u201d summary rather than via visible checked boxes in the filter panel (the relevant filter sections are sometimes out of frame). Individual study cards listing U.S. cities/states is not the same as the \u201cUnited States\u201d location filter being visibly applied.",
      "1": "Sorting is controlled via a \u201cDisplay\u201d panel where the site presents radio options like \u201cRelevance\u201d and \u201cNewest First\u201d; the UI in screenshots does not explicitly label the sort as \u201cLast Update Posted.\u201d In multiple screenshots where the Display panel is visible, \u201cRelevance\u201d is selected and \u201cNewest First\u201d is unselected. In other screenshots the Display panel is closed and no on-page indicator confirms the current sort order, and the result cards/rows shown typically do not display \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d dates, making sort verification impossible from those views alone.",
      "2": "In results views (card or table), the first displayed study\u2019s NCT, title, and a green \u201cRecruiting\u201d badge are visible, but the \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d date is generally not shown on the results listing itself in the provided screenshots. A separate \u201cStudy Record\u201d page does display \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d as a field in the header area (e.g., for NCT07282743 it shows \u201cLast Update Posted 2026-03-18\u201d), but that page does not display the ordered list context or any sort controls.",
      "3": "The second displayed result can be identified in some result-list screenshots by NCT number, title, and \u201cRecruiting\u201d badge (e.g., NCT07340320 appears as the second row in a table view in one screenshot). However, the \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d date is not visible on the results list in the screenshots, so it cannot be read directly for the second result from those list views. Study-record pages would show it, but those pages do not show the list ordering/sort state.",
      "4": "A third result is sometimes partially visible at the bottom of the card list (e.g., NCT07029009), but the title is truncated and no \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d date appears on the card in the captured area. None of the result-list screenshots show a \u201cLast Update Posted\u201d field for the third entry, so completing all required fields for the third result would require opening its study record page (which would show the date) even though that would remove the visible list-order context.",
      "5": "The interface includes buttons/links like \u201cSave,\u201d \u201cDownload,\u201d \u201cRSS,\u201d and \u201cFind Contact Information,\u201d but the screenshots do not show any evidence of those being used (no dialogs, confirmations, or submission flows are visible). Several screenshots indicate continued navigation between list views and individual study record pages; this is not inherently prohibited, but the stopping condition depends on having filters and newest-first sorting visibly confirmed plus capturing the first three results with \u201cLast Update Posted,\u201d which is generally not visible on list cards/rows in the screenshots and is only clearly visible on individual study record pages."
    },
